Project Description
Project Title:
Secure Login and Logout Web Application with Selenium Automation Testing
Author: Marri Rajamani
Creation Date: 13/05/2026

1. Introduction
This project focuses on the design and development of a secure end‑to‑end web application that implements Login and Logout functionality using modern web technologies. The application is developed by integrating frontend, backend, database, and automation testing layers to demonstrate a complete real‑world software development lifecycle.
The primary objective of the project is to ensure secure user authentication, session management, and automated testing using industry‑standard tools and best practices.

2. Project Objective
The main objectives of this project are:

To design a user‑friendly login and logout interface
To implement secure authentication using a strong password hashing algorithm
To store and validate user credentials using an Oracle database
To manage user sessions securely in the backend
To automate functional testing using Selenium WebDriver
To demonstrate an end‑to‑end enterprise‑level application architecture


3. Technology Stack
Frontend

HTML – For designing the structure of login and dashboard pages
CSS – For styling and improving user interface and usability

Backend

Java – Business logic implementation
JSP / Servlets – Request handling and session management

Database

Oracle Database – Secure storage of user credentials

Testing Tool

Selenium WebDriver – Automated functional testing of login and logout flows


4. System Architecture Overview
The application follows a three‑tier architecture:


Presentation Layer (Frontend)
Handles user interaction through HTML forms and CSS‑styled pages.


Application Layer (Backend)
Processes login requests, validates credentials, applies security algorithms, and manages sessions.


Data Layer (Database)
Stores user details securely using hashed passwords.



5. Functional Description
Login Functionality

The user enters a username and password.
The backend validates credentials against the Oracle database.
Passwords are never stored or compared in plain text.
On successful authentication, a secure session is created.
The user is redirected to a protected dashboard page.

Logout Functionality

The user clicks the logout button.
The server invalidates the active session.
The user is redirected back to the login page.
Unauthorized access after logout is prevented.


6. Database Design
The database contains a USER_DETAILS table with fields such as:

USER_ID
USERNAME
PASSWORD_HASH
CREATED_DATE

Passwords are stored in encrypted/hashed format to prevent data leaks.

7. Security Implementation
To ensure application security, the following measures are implemented:

SHA‑256 password hashing algorithm
Session‑based authentication
Password masking in UI
SQL Injection prevention using Prepared Statements
Session invalidation on logout
Restricted access to protected pages

These mechanisms ensure confidentiality, integrity, and authentication.

8. Selenium Automation Testing
Selenium WebDriver is used to automate:

Valid login test case
Logout test case
Page navigation verification
UI element validation

Automation improves reliability, reduces manual effort, and ensures regression‑free releases.

9. Advantages of the System

Secure authentication mechanism
Modular and scalable architecture
Automated testing improves quality
Industry‑oriented technology stack
Easy to maintain and extend


10. Conclusion
This project successfully demonstrates the implementation of a secure, scalable, and testable web application using HTML, CSS, Java, Oracle Database, and Selenium. It reflects real‑world enterprise development standards and emphasizes security, automation, and clean architecture.
